{title: The Sons of Parosh}
{subtitle: Ezra 2:3; 8:3; 10:25; Nehemiah 7:8; 3:25; 10:14}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Cm7] |
| [Ebmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From [Bb]Babylon the dust has cleared [Gm7]
The [Cm7]list of names is finally [F7]near
Two [Bb]thousand one hundred sev-[Gm7]en-ty-two
The [Cm7]sons of Parosh [F7]start a[Bb]new
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
We came [Eb]back with Zerub[D#dim7]babel
To build [Dm7]the temple, [Gm7]to stand
The ge[Cm7]nealogy is written [F7]clear
In [Bb]the shadow of the [Bb]land
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Zechariah leads the [Gm7]group
One [Cm7]hundred fifty men to prove [F7]
The [Bb]lineage held [Gm7]through time and tide
With [Cm7]Ez[F7]ra we have ar[Bb]rived
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
We came [Eb]back with Zerub[F7/Eb]babel
To build [Dm7]the temple, [Gm7]to stand
The ge[Cm7]nealogy is written [F7]clear
In [Bb]the shadow of the [Eb]land
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Ramiah and Izziah [Dm7]stand
[Cm7]Malchijah and E[F7]lea[Bb]zar
Mi[Eb]jamin and Benaiah [Dm7]too
[Cm7]Names called out in [F7]view
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Peda[Bb]iah the son of Pa[Gm7]rosh
Re[Cm7]pairs the wall with care [F7]
[Bb]Beside the court of the [Gm7]guard
The [Cm7]tower rising [F7]high [Bb]there
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
We came [Eb]back with Zerub[F7/Eb]babel
To build [Dm7]the temple, [Gm7]to stand
The ge[Cm7]nealogy is written [F7]clear
In [Bb]the shadow of the [Eb][F7/Eb][Dm7][Gm7]land [Cm7][F7][Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The [Ebmaj7]covenant is sealed [Dm7]once more
The [Cm7]sons of Parosh forev[Bb]er
{end_of_verse}
